# ClassMind configuration.
#
# NOTHING IN THIS FILE IS REQUIRED. With no .env file at all, ClassMind runs in
# local mode: an embedded data store under .classmind/, lecture files on disk,
# and the demo classes created automatically on first use. No AWS account, no
# credentials, no Docker and no AI API key.
#
# To change a default, copy this file to .env.local (git-ignored) and uncomment
# what you need. Every value is server-only — never prefix one NEXT_PUBLIC_.

# Where local mode keeps its data: the store (data/store.json) and uploaded
# lecture files (materials/). Delete this directory to reset everything.
# CLASSMIND_DATA_DIR=.classmind

# Which backend to use. Leave unset for local mode.
#   local           embedded store (default)
#   postgres        PostgreSQL for data and uploads — what the hosted demo uses;
#                   needs DATABASE_URL (see docs/deploy-vercel.md)
#   dynamodb-local  the optional DynamoDB adapter against DynamoDB Local (Docker)
#   aws             real DynamoDB + S3 — see .env.aws.example and docs/aws-setup.md
# CLASSMIND_TARGET=local

# Only for CLASSMIND_TARGET=postgres. A connection string from your provider;
# never commit a real one.
# DATABASE_URL=postgresql://USER:PASSWORD@HOST/DB?sslmode=require

# Public-demo protections (rate limits, read-only demo lecture, notice). Not a
# secret; the hosted demo sets it to 1.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_CLASSMIND_PUBLIC_DEMO=1

# Authorises GET/POST /api/admin/reset-demo (Vercel Cron sends it). Hosted only.
# CRON_SECRET=

# Only for CLASSMIND_TARGET=dynamodb-local:
#   docker run -d -p 8000:8000 --name classmind-ddb amazon/dynamodb-local
#   npm run setup:table && npm run seed
# DYNAMODB_ENDPOINT=http://localhost:8000
# CLASSMIND_TABLE=classmind
# No credentials are needed or wanted here: the adapter supplies DynamoDB Local's
# dummy credentials itself, and a placeholder key in this file would be used to
# sign real AWS requests if you later switch to the aws target.
